"""TPS709-Q1 — TI 30 V, 150 mA low-Iq LDO (AEC-Q100) in WSON-6 (DRV).

Fixed-output-voltage selector for the TPS709-Q1 automotive LDO family.
All nine orderables share the same pinout, package (DRV / WSON-6, 2×2 mm),
datasheet, and performance — they differ only in the factory-trim output
voltage. Select with `output_voltage`; the matching silicon is chosen
automatically.

    output_voltage  MPN
    3.3 V           TPS70933QDRVRQ1   (default)
    5.0 V           TPS70950QDRVRQ1
    1.2 V           TPS70912QDRVRQ1
    1.5 V           TPS70915QDRVRQ1
    1.8 V           TPS70918QDRVRQ1
    2.5 V           TPS70925QDRVRQ1
    2.7 V           TPS70927QDRVRQ1
    2.8 V           TPS70928QDRVRQ1
    3.0 V           TPS70930QDRVRQ1

Circuit (datasheet §7 Application and Implementation)
- C_IN: 4.7 µF, 50 V X7R, 0805. §7.1.1 notes the input cap is not required
  for stability but is strongly recommended for input ripple rejection
  and transient response. 50 V rating covers the full 30 V Vin range
  including automotive load-dump transients with DC-bias headroom.
- C_OUT: 4.7 µF, 16 V X7R, 0603. §7.1.1 stability requirement: effective
  capacitance ≥ 2 µF for Vout < 1.5 V, ≥ 1.5 µF for Vout ≥ 1.5 V, with
  ESR 0 Ω–0.2 Ω and ≤ 47 µF. 4.7 µF ±10 % worst-case = 4.23 µF and
  meets the 2 µF "effective" threshold for the 1.2 V trim even after
  typical X7R DC-bias / temperature derating. 16 V rating covers all
  supported Vout up to 5 V.

Pin usage
- EN: exposed as a raw net. Datasheet §6.4.1 says EN may float to enable
  the device (internal pull-up); if driven externally, Vin_EN ≤ 6.5 V.
- NC (pins 2, 5): not connected in the symbol; omitted here.
- EPAD (pin 7): stacked with pin 3 in the symbol (both named GND); the
  single "GND" pin mapping wires both to the ground net.
"""

load("@stdlib/units.zen", "Voltage")

Capacitor = Module("@stdlib/generics/Capacitor.zen")

output_voltage = config(
    Voltage,
    default="3.3V",
    allowed=["1.2V", "1.5V", "1.8V", "2.5V", "2.7V", "2.8V", "3V", "3.3V", "5V"],
    help="Factory-trimmed output voltage.",
    optional=False,
)

VIN = io(Power(voltage="2.7V to 30V"))
VOUT = io(Power(voltage=output_voltage))
GND = io(Ground())
EN = io(Net(NotConnected()), optional=True, help="Drive low to shut down; floats high internally. V_EN ≤ 6.5 V.")

# Factory-trimmed silicon selection. Each MPN maps to one fixed output voltage;
# no alternates (each trim is unique).
_FAMILY = {
    Voltage("1.2V"): "TPS70912QDRVRQ1",
    Voltage("1.5V"): "TPS70915QDRVRQ1",
    Voltage("1.8V"): "TPS70918QDRVRQ1",
    Voltage("2.5V"): "TPS70925QDRVRQ1",
    Voltage("2.7V"): "TPS70927QDRVRQ1",
    Voltage("2.8V"): "TPS70928QDRVRQ1",
    Voltage("3V"): "TPS70930QDRVRQ1",
    Voltage("3.3V"): "TPS70933QDRVRQ1",
    Voltage("5V"): "TPS70950QDRVRQ1",
}

_mpn = _FAMILY[output_voltage]

Component(
    name="U1",
    symbol=Symbol(library="TPS709-Q1.kicad_sym", name=_mpn),
    pins={
        "IN": VIN,
        "OUT": VOUT,
        "GND": GND,
        "EN": EN,
    },
)

# Input bypass (datasheet §7.1.1 / §7.2). 50 V covers the full 30 V Vin
# range including automotive load-dump transients.
Capacitor(name="C_IN", value="4.7uF", package="0805", voltage="50V", P1=VIN, P2=GND)

# Output bulk required for stability (datasheet §7.1.1). 4.7 µF X7R 16 V
# comfortably meets the ≥2 µF effective-capacitance requirement for the
# 1.2 V trim worst case even after tolerance and DC-bias derating.
Capacitor(name="C_OUT", value="4.7uF", package="0603", voltage="16V", P1=VOUT, P2=GND)

Layout(name="TPS709-Q1", path="layout/TPS709-Q1")
